{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_broker_actor_base", "label": "BrokerActor base class", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/broker-actor-base.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_brokeractor", "label": "BrokerActor", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The abstract base owns everything shared across protocols \u2014 lifecycle state machine, outbound buffer, reconnect loop, subscriber tracking, desired subscriptions \u2014 so a subclass only writes the three protocol hooks.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/broker-actor-base.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_lifecycle_state_machine", "label": "Broker lifecycle state machine", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Four states \u2014 disconnected, connecting, connected, disconnecting. A connecting failure triggers the reconnect loop; stop transitions through disconnecting from any state.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/broker-actor-base.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_connectimplementation", "label": "connectImplementation hook", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/broker-actor-base.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_disconnectimplementation", "label": "disconnectImplementation hook", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Called on stop AND before every re-connect attempt, so a subclass never builds a new connection on top of the dead one's handles. That makes it an idempotent contract: it may run on an already-dead connection and must drop only live handles, never the desired subscriptions.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/broker-actor-base.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_dispatchoutgoing", "label": "dispatchOutgoing hook", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/broker-actor-base.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_outbound_buffer", "label": "Outbound buffer", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Bounded FIFO sized in messages (1000 default). On overflow the base always evicts the OLDEST envelope and publishes BrokerBufferOverflow rather than throwing; outboundBuffer:0 disables buffering and publishes BrokerNotConnected instead.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/broker-actor-base.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_subscriber_tracking", "label": "Subscriber tracking and fan-out", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "subscribeRef registers a ref for a topic and death-watches it; unsubscribeRef matches on the ref's PATH rather than the object, so holding a different ref for the same actor still unsubscribes.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/broker-actor-base.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_pruneterminatedsubscriber", "label": "pruneTerminatedSubscriber and the mandatory Terminated arm", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "onReceive is abstract, so the base never sees a message and cannot act on the watch it started. Without the Terminated arm a stopped subscriber stays in every topic and costs a dead-lettered tell on each fan-out \u2014 a real defect (#1111). It deliberately does not unwatch: the cell already dropped the watch when it delivered Terminated.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/broker-actor-base.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_desired_subscriptions", "label": "Desired subscriptions", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The set of subscriptions held ON THE BROKER is kept separate from the live handles so it outlives any one connection: a runtime subscribe survives a reconnect, one issued while disconnected lands on the next connect, option seeding is once-only so a runtime unsubscribe is not resurrected, and a subscription that cannot be established is a warning rather than a dead connection. The replay is driven by the subclass because the right point in the handshake is protocol-specific (kafkajs wants every subscribe in before consumer.run).", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/broker-actor-base.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_reconnect_with_backoff", "label": "Reconnect with backoff", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Each attempt waits min(initialDelayMs * factor^(attempt-1), maxDelayMs) times a random 1 +/- randomFactor. The jitter is what keeps a fleet from retrying in lockstep \u2014 without it every actor that lost the same broker wakes in the same millisecond, wave after wave, and the herd can hold the recovering broker down.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/broker-actor-base.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_circuit_breaker", "label": "Circuit-breaker reset jitter", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "When the breaker is open the actor re-checks somewhere in [resetMs, resetMs x (1 + randomFactor)]. That jitter is one-sided \u2014 a breaker is never re-tried early.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/broker-actor-base.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_lifecycle_events", "label": "Broker lifecycle events", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "BrokerConnected / BrokerDisconnected / BrokerReconnectAttempt / BrokerReconnectFailed / BrokerBufferOverflow / BrokerNotConnected are published on system.eventStream and carry actorPath, so one monitor can watch every broker actor uniformly.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/broker-actor-base.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_settings_resolution", "label": "Broker settings resolution", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "preStart merges builtInDefaultOptions < readOptionsFromConfig (HOCON) < constructor argument, validates against requiredOptions and stashes the result. A missing required setting throws in preStart, so the actor goes through the supervisor's failure path before it ever attempts to connect.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/broker-actor-base.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_broker_actor_base", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_brokeractor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/io/broker-actor-base.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_broker_actor_base", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_io_broker_actor_base_lifecycle_state_machine", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "